766
00:57:50,920 --> 00:57:57,380
And the root test is OK with
that, whereas that test wasn't

767
00:57:57,380 --> 00:57:58,380
OK with that.

768
00:57:58,380 --> 00:58:00,420
So the root test.

769
00:58:00,420 --> 00:58:05,020
So you have a series,
again, like this.

770
00:58:05,020 --> 00:58:08,780
And the root test is
that you're looking

771
00:58:08,780 --> 00:58:13,860
at-- you're taking the
absolute value of this

772
00:58:13,860 --> 00:58:16,700
and then you're
taking the n-th root.

773
00:58:16,700 --> 00:58:20,540
So this means-- this is
the same as saying a n

774
00:58:20,540 --> 00:58:26,180
absolute value, if you want to
