990
01:16:27,180 --> 01:16:32,080
So x is fixed, and I'm not
interested in x equal to 0.

991
01:16:32,080 --> 01:16:36,840
I'm assuming that x is not
equal to 0, because when x is 0,

992
01:16:36,840 --> 01:16:38,420
this here is just--

993
01:16:38,420 --> 01:16:44,780
it's only for-- x to the power
of 0 is by definition one.

994
01:16:44,780 --> 01:16:50,540
And all the other things,
all the other terms, are 0.

995
01:16:50,540 --> 01:16:53,380
So this here is-- it's
definitely converging

996
01:16:53,380 --> 01:16:55,360
when x is equal to 0.

997
01:16:55,360 --> 01:16:58,425
So let's not look at that.

998
01:16:58,425 --> 01:17:00,300
And then-- because if
you don't look at that,

999
01:17:00,300 --> 01:17:02,900
you can look at-- you
can think about a n.

1000
01:17:02,900 --> 01:17:08,660
You can now think about,
sorry, as the series

1001
01:17:08,660 --> 01:17:14,780
where bn is x to the
power n over n factorial.

1002
01:17:14,780 --> 01:17:17,180
If you think about
this thing here,

1003
01:17:17,180 --> 01:17:19,950
and you think about
the series as now bn,

1004
01:17:19,950 --> 01:17:23,590
then the ratio test
tells you that if you're

1005
01:17:23,590 --> 01:17:29,280
looking at the ratio
of bn plus 1 over bn--

1006
01:17:35,270 --> 01:17:40,510
so if you're looking
at bn plus 1 over bn,

1007
01:17:40,510 --> 01:17:43,070
you take the absolute
value of this here.

1008
01:17:43,070 --> 01:17:47,630
Well, this is just
x to the power n

1009
01:17:47,630 --> 01:17:52,650
plus 1 over n plus 1 factorial.

1010
01:17:52,650 --> 01:17:57,190
And then you have to
divide it by x to the power

1011
01:17:57,190 --> 01:18:00,070
n over n factorial.

1012
01:18:00,070 --> 01:18:05,630
But if you do that, this
here flips upside down,

1013
01:18:05,630 --> 01:18:10,510
and you're getting x to
the power n plus 1 times

1014
01:18:10,510 --> 01:18:12,430
n factorial.

1015
01:18:12,430 --> 01:18:18,170
And then you're getting x to
the n times n plus 1 factorial.

1016
01:18:18,170 --> 01:18:21,330
So this is what it's equal to.

1017
01:18:21,330 --> 01:18:24,410
And now, of course,
here, there are

1018
01:18:24,410 --> 01:18:27,930
x times itself n plus 1 times.

1019
01:18:27,930 --> 01:18:31,750
The n of those is
canceling out with this.

1020
01:18:31,750 --> 01:18:34,890
So this is x.

1021
01:18:34,890 --> 01:18:41,170
And here, you see here
the n plus 1 factorial.

1022
01:18:41,170 --> 01:18:45,890
You can write as n
plus 1 and then times

1023
01:18:45,890 --> 01:18:48,130
n times n minus 1 cetera.

1024
01:18:48,130 --> 01:18:50,610
But that's just n factorial.

1025
01:18:50,610 --> 01:18:52,250
So you can write it like that.

1026
01:18:52,250 --> 01:18:56,050
And so you see that
this here cancels that.

1027
01:18:56,050 --> 01:18:59,250
So you're left with n plus 1.

1028
01:18:59,250 --> 01:19:06,130
Remember, if x is fixed as n
goes to infinity, this here--

1029
01:19:06,130 --> 01:19:10,390
for each fixed x,
this just goes to 0.

1030
01:19:10,390 --> 01:19:15,430
So now you have, from the
ratio test, if that limit--

1031
01:19:15,430 --> 01:19:18,270
if it has a limit--
it does have a limit.

1032
01:19:18,270 --> 01:19:23,890
If that limit is strictly less
than 1, but it's actually 0.

1033
01:19:23,890 --> 01:19:26,530
So it's definitely
fallen under 1.

1034
01:19:26,530 --> 01:19:28,670
So it's convergent.

1035
01:19:28,670 --> 01:19:32,990
So the ratio test tells you--

1036
01:19:32,990 --> 01:19:39,890
so by the ratio test,
this is convergent.

1037
01:19:46,694 --> 01:19:49,350
And so we'll finish here.

